Z||000000||ray b||06-17-2001||02:37 PM||||are all poly bushings for the fiero the same<BR>hardness or are softer ones available?<BR>i would like better control but not to be beat up by toooo stiff bushings.<BR>story in autoweek said that poly bushings are made in various grades from equal to stock rubber to very hard for race or auto-X.<BR>as i now have two 88's that have a softer ride i don't want to make too stiff as some have complained about.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||06-18-2001||08:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>are all poly bushings for the fiero the same<BR>hardness or are softer ones available?<BR>i would like better control but not to be beat up by toooo stiff bushings.<BR>story in autoweek said that poly bushings are made in various grades from equal to stock rubber to very hard for race or auto-X.<BR>as i now have two 88's that have a softer ride i don't want to make too stiff as some have complained about.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know about Fiero bushings, but my father got a set of poly diff mounts for his 280Z. They were too hard and made the interior too buzzy, so he asked the company to pour him a set of softer ones. They did. I'll ask him what company it was tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||06-18-2001||12:48 PM||||I don't know what grade of hardness my poly bushings are, but the ride with them is not overly harsh.  I do notice a little more rattling over large bumps because the suspension can't deflect rearward like it could before.  No squeaks in 5000 miles.  I put them on my 88GT.||||reg||1
