Z||000005||Eric||06-19-2001||08:05 AM||||I think they were Energy Suspension, the same brand the Fiero Store sells.  I used the black ones, but I doubt the color makes a difference.  I traded every rubber bushing on the car for poly.  You could probably also make an arguement because the 88's suspension is fundamentally better, harder compound bushings won't affect ride quality as much as previous years.<p>[This message has been edited by Eric (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||HarryG||06-19-2001||12:00 PM||||A couple weeks ago, I asked a mfgr's rep for Energy Suspension about them offering the same bushing in hard or soft versions. He said he thought they were headed in that direction, but could offer no time to production. Right now, the only ones I've seen in their catalog with hard/soft versions are their Universal Mounts.<P>||||reg||1
